/benchmarks/botbench/results/
# Real-world GPS source tracks for the real-track arm. NOT redistributed here:
# the SondeHub radiosonde/amateur tracks are CC BY-SA 2.0, and this project does
# not ship copyleft data. The PX4 drone logs are CC-BY (attribution only) and
# could be tracked, but the set is kept whole and local so the arm has one
# provenance story. Every file is re-fetchable from the APIs documented in
# benchmarks/botbench/real-tracks/README.md, and each scenario commits to the
# exact bytes it was cut from via a sha256 in its segment provenance.
/benchmarks/botbench/real-tracks/
# JetBrains IDE project state (bot.iml, workspace.xml and friends). Per-user
# and per-machine, so it belongs to whoever opened the repo, not to the repo.
.idea/


# Local code-review / audit reports (not part of the codebase)
/CODE-REVIEW-*.md

# Former home of the working notes, now private/notes/ (see below). Kept as a
# tripwire: nothing should be written here any more, and if something is, it
# must still never be committed or published (webpack.common.js skips it too).
/docs/temp/

# The PRIVATE nested repository: agent instructions, Claude/Codex commands and
# skills, working notes, probes, in-progress analysis and review reports. It has
# its own .git and its own branches (wt pairs them with this repo's worktrees).
# Ignored, never a submodule: a gitlink here would publish its commit hash and
# break every public clone. The pre-commit hook refuses it even with `git add -f`.
/private/

# Solar/lunar alignment reference photographs, for checking refraction and
# celestial positions against real images with known camera position and time.
# Third-party photographs (Wikimedia Commons) — local only, not redistributed.
/alignment-tests/

# Local AI-agent skills and configuration
/.agents

# Working directory of the user-data egress check (scripts/security-scan-egress.mjs)
.egress/
